    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xst9o7s",
      "content": "Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) are guidelines to the government for creating a just and welfare-oriented society. They are contained in Part IV of the Constitution of India (Articles 36–51). Although they are not enforceable by courts, they are fundamental in the governance of the country.<img></img>"
    },
