      "id": "ju3dzjx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Difference between Fundamental Rights and DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 37 explicitly declares that DPSPs are non-justiciable, yet fundamental in the governance of the country.",
        "Article 40 (Organization of Village Panchayats) is a key Gandhian principle frequently asked in Prelims.",
        "Article 44 (Uniform Civil Code) belongs to the Liberal–Intellectual principles category.",
        "Minerva Mills Case (1980) established that the Indian Constitution is founded on the bedrock of balance between Fundamental Rights and DPSPs."
      ],
      "id": "ld2rdg9"
    },
